# Hullrot: Eclipsion

Welcome to [bold]Hullrot: Eclipsion[/bold]. This is a roleplay server set in the [bold]Taypan asteroid belt[/bold], and every player here helps shape its story.

Before anything else, know that this is [bold]not[/bold] a deathmatch server. What you do matters. Your choices, your words, and the people you meet all leave a mark on the world. Play your character honestly, stay in the moment, and treat the setting as a place you live in rather than a scoreboard you climb.

[head=2][color=#e8b04b]What kind of place this is[/color][/head]

Taypan is harsh and unforgiving. You will lose fights, you will die, and sometimes you will lose gear you cared about. That is part of the experience, not a sign you did something wrong. Take the loss, adapt, and keep the story moving.

Conflict belongs here too. Betrayal, sabotage, and destruction can all create moments people remember for a long time. But the best moments come from variety. Blowing up the same reactor or killing the same enemy every round turns a rich world into a repetitive grind, so look for the choice that makes a better story instead of the fastest kill.

Out here in the belt, a few things are worth remembering:

- A living prisoner opens more doors than a dead enemy.
- A conversation can be more memorable than a firefight.
- Your character's decisions ripple out and affect everyone around them.

[head=2][color=#e8b04b]Read the rules before you play[/color][/head]

The full rules live in the in-game [textlink="Roleplay Rules" link="RoleplayRules"]. Please read them before your first round. They cover:

- What we expect from roleplay
- Mutiny and turning on your own faction
- Round Removal (RR)
- Hate speech, and how in-character species and faction conflict works

You can open the Guidebook at any time with [color=#6ab7d6][bold]Numpad 0[/bold][/color], or the [bold]Guidebook[/bold] button in the game menu.

[head=2][color=#e8b04b]Learn the setting[/color][/head]

Eclipsion has its own history, factions, and politics that will not match anything you know from standard Space Station 14. Start with [textlink="Your First Round" link="GettingStarted"] and [textlink="Factions" link="Factions"], then use the [textlink="Lore" link="Lore"] section when you want the deeper setting. It covers:

- The history of the Taypan belt and the wider universe
- The major factions and what they are fighting for
- Current conflicts and the political situation
- Important places and events
- The technology, culture, and tone of the setting

Knowing the setting helps you build a character who fits into it and understand why the conflicts around you are happening.

[head=2][color=#e8b04b]Learn the mechanics[/color][/head]

Eclipsion runs many custom systems that change how the game plays. You do not need to master all of them before you jump in, but a quick read of [textlink="Custom Controls" link="Tutorial"] and [textlink="Economy, Ships, and Combat" link="HullrotSystems"] will help you survive your first rounds and pull your weight for your faction. The Guidebook explains:

- The combat system and how firearms work
- Melee fighting
- The economy and faction systems
- The unique features that make this server its own thing

Take your time, explore the Guidebook, and become part of the story of Taypan.
